			<!-- Category Descriptions -->
			<trans-unit id="categories.GSB.style.colors.background.description">
				<source>Here you can define up to six color values that will shape the corporate design (CD) of the website. These colors are then available for selection in content elements where a background color can be set. The "Color value name" field should assign a custom name or designation for a specific color value. Instead of remembering complicated hex codes, the editorial team can assign an easily understandable name for the color, such as "Pigeon Blue" or "Accent Color".</source>
			</trans-unit>

			<trans-unit id="categories.GSB.style.colors.colorGeneral.description">
				<source>The values for the color variables can be exchanged at this point. These are then used in the CSS. This allows, for example, the button color or footer to be adjusted.</source>
			</trans-unit>

			<trans-unit id="categories.GSB.style.favicons.description">
				<source>Please use the service at: https://realfavicongenerator.net/ (This service is free and copyright-free). For this you only need a 512x512 large favicon PNG image and have it processed by this service. Download the generated files and add them e.g. under /fileadmin/Favicons/. Then you can link the corresponding files here again to exchange your favicon. Of course you can also create all files manually. The file names and image sizes must be maintained.</source>
			</trans-unit>

